            "created_at": "2025-08-13T08:20:16.507801+00:00",
            "notes": "Typically, we start with [Shield Stampede](item_0c4ef690-6472-48fe-9257-864c4381f584) to be able to charge and pin enemies without getting melted instantly. Don't overdo it, stick to corners and cover. Focus mainly on getting Firestrikes out. If an opportunity presents itself to charge into the backline and peel off a healer or DPS, go for it. Typically it is good to fall back after a charge as you lack the melee power and sustain from more brawl-oriented builds. Combined with the AP you will probably get a few (pin) kills.\n\nYou may find yourself against an [Orisa](hero_91644d44-1093-4f62-ac51-020975465e85) who will probably either Fortify or stop you with her spear. The latter we can not do much against but we can choose  [Vroom Boom Boom](item_b016a02c-50bd-4010-91bb-661c1101ade7) to inflict damage onto a Fortified [Orisa](hero_91644d44-1093-4f62-ac51-020975465e85). It depends on your playstyle but you may want to consider going for  [Impact Burst](item_01fa37d8-4355-4ec2-a9af-59bf030e2882) or [Magma Strike](item_6d8d893f-d161-4e10-a084-4a5749b12990) instead to damage from a distance.\n\nIf you're encountering [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6) you can stick to [Shield Stampede](item_0c4ef690-6472-48fe-9257-864c4381f584) but be aware that a good [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6) will be able to absorb many of your Firestrikes. In that case, maybe resort to [Magma Strike](item_6d8d893f-d161-4e10-a084-4a5749b12990) or prioritize [Vroom Boom Boom](item_b016a02c-50bd-4010-91bb-661c1101ade7) in your build.",
